WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.664
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:09.211
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.511 --> 00:00:15.843
Unit thirty-eight: Sequencing and Time Linkers. Today you will tell a story in order with first, then and finally.

4
00:00:16.143 --> 00:00:18.865
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.696
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.261
First.

7
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.797
First means at the beginning.

8
00:00:27.383 --> 00:00:28.640
First, I woke up.

9
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.926
Your turn. Say: First.

10
00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:35.559
First.

11
00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:37.074
Then.

12
00:00:38.083 --> 00:00:39.537
Then means after that.

13
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.244
Then I washed.

14
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.514
Your turn. Say: Then.

15
00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:48.101
Then.

16
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:49.886
After that.

17
00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:53.475
After that means following the previous event.

18
00:00:54.083 --> 00:00:55.479
After that, I ate.

19
00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:58.689
Your turn. Say: After that.

20
00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:02.627
After that.

21
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:04.361
Meanwhile.

22
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.199
Meanwhile means at the same time.

23
00:01:07.783 --> 00:01:09.226
Meanwhile, she cooked.

24
00:01:09.817 --> 00:01:12.295
Your turn. Say: Meanwhile.

25
00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.251
Meanwhile.

26
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:18.145
Eventually.

27
00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.509
Eventually means after a long time.

28
00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:23.780
Eventually we arrived.

29
00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:27.105
Your turn. Say: Eventually.

30
00:01:29.967 --> 00:01:31.072
Eventually.

31
00:01:31.817 --> 00:01:32.713
Finally.

32
00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:35.287
Finally means at the end.

33
00:01:35.883 --> 00:01:37.210
Finally, I left.

34
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:40.190
Your turn. Say: Finally.

35
00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:43.907
Finally.

36
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:45.523
In the end.

37
00:01:46.517 --> 00:01:48.586
In the end means as a final result.

38
00:01:49.183 --> 00:01:50.591
In the end, we won.

39
00:01:51.183 --> 00:01:53.406
Your turn. Say: In the end.

40
00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.221
In the end.

41
00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.124
Afterwards.

42
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:01.756
Afterwards means later.

43
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.384
Afterwards, we rested.

44
00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:07.705
Your turn. Say: Afterwards.

45
00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:11.719
Afterwards.

46
00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:16.149
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:20.562
Visal, tell the story of your morning using time linkers.

48
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:32.484
First, I woke up at six. Then I brushed my teeth. After that, I had breakfast. Meanwhile, my mother prepared lunch. Finally, I left for school.

49
00:02:33.583 --> 00:02:35.049
What do the linkers do?

50
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:51.146
They show the order of events and help the listener follow the story. First, then and after that are simple. Eventually and in the end show a longer process or result.

51
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.681
How do we punctuate them?

52
00:02:54.783 --> 00:03:09.315
A linker at the start of a sentence takes a comma: Finally, we arrived. Meanwhile means at the same time, so it joins two parallel actions. Afterwards means later and goes at the end or beginning.

53
00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.176
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.017 --> 00:03:17.361
Grammar focus: Sequencing: first, then, after that, meanwhile, finally.

55
00:03:17.661 --> 00:03:18.802
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.517 --> 00:03:21.563
First, I woke up at six.

57
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:24.577
Meanwhile, my mother prepared lunch.

58
00:03:25.483 --> 00:03:27.193
Finally, I left for school.

59
00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:35.383
Use first, then, after that, meanwhile, eventually and finally to order events. Put a comma after a linker at the start of a sentence.

60
00:03:36.117 --> 00:03:40.325
Be careful! Don't say: Finally, I woke up, then slept.

61
00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:45.091
Say: First, I woke up; then I washed.

62
00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.228
Choose the right order linker.

63
00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.848
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:51.633 --> 00:03:52.809
Telling It in Order.

65
00:03:53.109 --> 00:03:55.781
First, I woke up at six and brushed my teeth.

66
00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.755
Then I had breakfast with my family.

67
00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:02.335
Meanwhile, my mother prepared lunch for school.

68
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:05.948
After that, I rode my bicycle to class.

69
00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:10.349
Eventually I arrived, and finally the lesson began.

70
00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:15.389
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.389
blank I woke up, and then I washed.

72
00:04:18.689 --> 00:04:22.052
A, Finally. B, First. C, Meanwhile.

73
00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.530
The answer is B: First.

74
00:04:28.683 --> 00:04:31.951
I cooked. blank, she set the table. (at the same time)

75
00:04:32.251 --> 00:04:35.870
A, Meanwhile. B, Afterwards. C, Finally.

76
00:04:39.433 --> 00:04:41.712
The answer is A: Meanwhile.

77
00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.105
blank, we arrived after three hours.

78
00:04:45.405 --> 00:04:49.116
A, Eventually. B, Firstly then. C, Meanwhile.

79
00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:54.782
The answer is A: Eventually.

80
00:04:55.917 --> 00:04:57.614
Which linker shows the end?

81
00:04:57.914 --> 00:05:01.707
A, First. B, Finally. C, Meanwhile.

82
00:05:05.267 --> 00:05:07.568
The answer is B: Finally.

83
00:05:08.717 --> 00:05:11.459
According to the reading, how did the writer go to class?

84
00:05:11.759 --> 00:05:15.691
A, by bicycle. B, by bus. C, on foot.

85
00:05:19.233 --> 00:05:21.686
The answer is A: by bicycle.

86
00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:26.075
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:26.917 --> 00:05:30.042
Tell the story of your morning using at least four time linkers.

88
00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.327
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:40.627 --> 00:05:53.771
First, I woke up at six. Then I washed my face. After that, I ate breakfast while my mother prepared lunch. Finally, I left for school. I use linkers to put the events in order.

90
00:05:54.071 --> 00:05:55.862
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:03.570
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and sequencing: first, then, after that, meanwhile, finally.

92
00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:08.531
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

93
00:06:08.831 --> 00:06:12.006
